  "description": "AHAFOF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C16 H68 Ho6 N16 O23 8+,8(Cl1 1-),2(C4 H8 N4),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho1A (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2A (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3A (Ho) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.437-5.187 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.35-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ho6(μ6-O)(μ3-OH)8(L)4(H2O)14]Cl8·2L·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 14 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 14 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
